2026-10-15T16:09:47.1039448Z 
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1039525Z 1. expiry
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1092647Z   ok     a freshly created key with a 1-day lifetime authenticates
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1099981Z   ok     the same key is refused once its expiry has passed
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1100223Z 
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1100320Z 2. clamped to the configured maximum
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1119308Z   ok     a requested lifetime of 5365 days is clamped to the configured maximum of 365 days (expires 2027-10-15T16:09:47.109996Z)
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1120300Z 
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1120781Z 3. no lifetime given -> the configured maximum, not the old non-expiring default
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1137015Z   ok     a key created with no lifetime argument gets the configured maximum (expires 2027-10-15T16:09:47.111890Z)
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1138769Z   ok     and specifically not the year 2999 - regular keys no longer default to practically-never-expiring
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1139119Z 
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1139189Z 4. rotation
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1172785Z   ok     the successor is a fresh random value, not the same key
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1173271Z   ok     and a new row
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1175244Z   ok     the successor records which key it replaces
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1175555Z   ok     the successor carries the predecessor's description
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1175846Z   ok     and the same key type
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1191651Z   ok     the predecessor keeps authenticating right after rotation - no gap
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1205351Z   ok     and the successor already authenticates - both work at once, by the caller's choice
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1220503Z   ok     the predecessor is refused once explicitly retired (deleted)
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1225990Z   ok     the successor is unaffected by retiring its predecessor - ON DELETE SET NULL, not CASCADE
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1229309Z   ok     the successor's lineage pointer is nulled rather than the row being taken down with its predecessor
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1229676Z 
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1229793Z 5. rotation is refused for a special-purpose key
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1248579Z   ok     rotating a calendar key through the new path is refused rather than silently handled
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1248805Z 
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1248901Z 6. special-purpose key types keep their year-2999 expiry
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1251955Z   ok     a calendar key created via CreateApiKey() is still practically non-expiring
2026-10-15T16:09:47.1267526Z   ok     and so is a label-worker-type key created the same way, even though LabelWorkerCredentialService never actually calls CreateApiKey() for real ones
