2026-10-15T16:24:47.1494669Z  2026-10-15 16:18:58.573 UTC [4698] STATEMENT:  -- Issue #552 (#487 remediation), maintainer decision D4, modelled on ADR-0029
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1495067Z  	-- (docs/adr/0029-stock-locations-reference-existing-locations.md) and the migration that
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1495424Z  	-- implemented it (migrations/0288.pgsql.sql): add the foreign keys the baseline never gave
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1495742Z  	-- any of products' six upstream reference columns - location_id, qu_id_purchase,
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1496011Z  	-- qu_id_stock, qu_id_consume, qu_id_price, product_group_id.
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1496199Z  	--
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1496397Z  	-- NO AUTOMATIC REPAIR: ABORT WITH A REPORT, BY MAINTAINER DECISION. Two paths reach these
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1496662Z  	-- columns, and they are handled separately:
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1496925Z  	--   * Upgrading an existing Victual installation runs this migration over live data. Before
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1497266Z  	--     this migration nothing refused deleting a location, quantity unit or product group that
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1497603Z  	--     a product still named, so a product can already hold a dangling reference. The preflight
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1497940Z  	--     below lists every affected product, column and missing id, and aborts the upgrade before
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1498272Z  	--     any foreign key is added, exactly as 0288 does for stock.location_id. Nothing is changed
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1498572Z  	--     or invented; the operator repairs the data and reruns the migration.
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1498886Z  	--   * A legacy Grocy import copies into a blank database; services/Database/DatabaseImporter.php's
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1499235Z  	--     AssertProductReferences() reports and refuses there, before truncation (ADR-0029's
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1499575Z  	--     import precedent).
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1499715Z  	--
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1499919Z  	-- ON DELETE RESTRICT ON UPDATE RESTRICT NOT DEFERRABLE on every one of the six, exactly as
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1500253Z  	-- 0288's stock_location_id_fkey. No cascade, no automatic repair on a future delete. A future
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1500668Z  	-- violation reaches GenericEntityApiController::DeleteObject()'s existing generic 23503
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1501007Z  	-- handling (issue #515/PR #551) and answers the documented 400, same as every other enforced
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1501305Z  	-- foreign key in this tree (see tests/Pgsql/ReferenceRefusalTest.php,
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1501552Z  	-- tests/Pgsql/ProductReferenceIntegrityTest.php).
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1501834Z  	-- Bounded blocking, as 0288 does: the index builds and FK additions take write-blocking locks.
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1502087Z  	SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '5s';
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1502248Z  	SET LOCAL statement_timeout = '60s';
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1502503Z  	LOCK TABLE products, locations, quantity_units, product_groups IN SHARE ROW EXCLUSIVE MODE;
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1502749Z  	
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1502944Z  	-- Upstream Grocy stores 0 in qu_id_consume and qu_id_price to mean "unset" (its migrations
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1503266Z  	-- 0210/0219 test IFNULL(x, 0) = 0), and databases imported before the importer translated it
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1503590Z  	-- (PR #624) may still carry that 0. It is upstream's own meaning, not a dangling reference, so
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1503904Z  	-- it becomes NULL here exactly as the importer now does. No other value is changed.
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1504190Z  	UPDATE products SET qu_id_consume = NULL WHERE qu_id_consume = 0;
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1504438Z  	UPDATE products SET qu_id_price = NULL WHERE qu_id_price = 0;
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1504629Z  	
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1504733Z  	DO $$
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1504841Z  	DECLARE
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1504953Z  	    ref record;
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1505082Z  	    dangling_count bigint;
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1505226Z  	    sample text;
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1505447Z  	    report text := '';
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1505588Z  	    total bigint := 0;
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1505718Z  	BEGIN
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1505838Z  	    FOR ref IN SELECT * FROM (VALUES
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1506000Z  	        ('location_id', 'locations'),
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1506172Z  	        ('qu_id_purchase', 'quantity_units'),
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1506353Z  	        ('qu_id_stock', 'quantity_units'),
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1506419Z  	        ('qu_id_consume', 'quantity_units'),
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1506479Z  	        ('qu_id_price', 'quantity_units'),
