2026-10-15T16:24:47.1518932Z  2026-10-15 16:19:00.400 UTC [4708] CONTEXT:  PL/pgSQL function inline_code_block line 15 at RAISE
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1519156Z  2026-10-15 16:19:00.400 UTC [4708] STATEMENT:  -- Issue #492 (H3, #487 remediation): "Stock edits accept negative quantities and fractional
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1519289Z  	-- consumption leaves residue". ADR-0032 decision 4 and acceptance gate 6 require
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1519430Z  	-- EditStockEntry() to refuse a negative amount, and commit 2039d5947 ("fix: apply ADR-0032
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1519561Z  	-- stock amount policy") already applied that refusal - and the matching refusal in
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1519714Z  	-- AddProduct(), ConsumeProduct(), InventoryProduct(), OpenProduct() and TransferProduct() -
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1519881Z  	-- in PHP. Nothing in the schema itself backed that up: `stock.amount` (db/pgsql/baseline/01_tables.sql)
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1520007Z  	-- carries no CHECK, so any writer that does not go through StockService - a future
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1520156Z  	-- application bug, a direct import path, a hand-written migration or maintenance script -
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1520287Z  	-- can still persist a negative row.
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1520406Z  	--
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1520543Z  	-- This adds the database-level backstop the issue asks for: `amount >= 0`. Zero stays
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1520671Z  	-- writable on purpose. Issue #487's "Corrections to the audit" item 3 records that
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1520813Z  	-- WeighLocation() legitimately zeroes a vessel's stock row when its gross reading equals
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1520962Z  	-- its tare weight (services/StockService.php's WeighLocation() call into EditStockEntry()
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1521095Z  	-- with $newAmount = 0), and ADR-0032 open question 1 leaves "no row may hold 0" undecided
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1521230Z  	-- and out of scope for this record. `stock_measurement_coherence_check` (migration 0275)
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1521368Z  	-- already requires exactly `amount = 1` for an opened, measured row - a strictly narrower
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1521462Z  	-- constraint than `amount >= 0`, so the two never conflict.
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1521511Z  	--
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1521657Z  	-- `stock_log.amount` is deliberately left unconstrained: TRANSACTION_TYPE_TRANSFER_FROM and
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1521797Z  	-- TRANSACTION_TYPE_CONSUME bookings store a negative amount by design (the ledger records
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1521923Z  	-- the signed delta a booking applies, not a resulting balance) - see the constant
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1522076Z  	-- documentation in services/StockService.php. Only `stock` (the resulting balance per row)
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1522139Z  	-- gets the non-negative constraint.
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1522184Z  	--
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1522315Z  	-- **Import vs upgrade (maintainer correction, 2026-09-29).** DatabaseImporter's own
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1522472Z  	-- AssertStockAmounts()/SourceColumnExpression() (services/Database/DatabaseImporter.php)
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1522713Z  	-- validate a *legacy import*, which lands in a blank, freshly migrated database - there is
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1522866Z  	-- no existing installation to run this migration over in that path. An *app upgrade* is the
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1523007Z  	-- other path: this migration runs against an existing installation's live data, which can
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1523148Z  	-- already hold a negative stock.amount row - issue #492's own defect is exactly how one
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1523287Z  	-- could get there before this fix existed. Adding the CHECK straight onto that data would
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1523428Z  	-- fail with a raw PostgreSQL SQLSTATE 23514 naming no row and explaining nothing, the same
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1523565Z  	-- shape of unhelpful failure the importer's own preflight was added to avoid. ADR-0029's
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1523704Z  	-- pattern - a read-only preflight that lists the offending rows and aborts with a clear
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1523840Z  	-- report before the constraint is added - is the maintainer's standing rule for exactly
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1523973Z  	-- this, followed here the way migration 0288 already follows it for a dangling stock
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1524109Z  	-- location. No repair invents a value nobody recorded; the one exception is the same one
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1524245Z  	-- the maintainer decided for the importer: a residue within ADR-0032's tolerance of zero
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1524390Z  	-- (StockService::AMOUNT_TOLERANCE = 1e-9; the literal below MUST match that constant, this
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1524534Z  	-- migration cannot reference it directly) counts as zero, because CompareAmounts() already
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1524664Z  	-- treats it as zero everywhere else at runtime and refusing an upgrade over it would be
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1524749Z  	-- refusing over a value nobody would call negative.
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1524809Z  	SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '5s';
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1524872Z  	SET LOCAL statement_timeout = '60s';
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1524946Z  	LOCK TABLE stock IN SHARE ROW EXCLUSIVE MODE;
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1524994Z  	
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1525211Z  	-- Zeroes only a residue within tolerance - see the docblock above for why this one case
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1525355Z  	-- is a translation rather than a refusal. Every amount at or below -1e-9 is untouched here
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1525463Z  	-- and is what the DO block below inspects and, if any remain, refuses on.
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1525569Z  	UPDATE stock SET amount = 0 WHERE amount < 0 AND amount >= -1e-9;
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1525618Z  	
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1525666Z  	DO $$
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1525713Z  	DECLARE
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1525771Z  	    negative_count bigint;
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1525823Z  	    sample text;
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1525869Z  	BEGIN
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1525976Z  	    SELECT count(*) INTO negative_count FROM stock WHERE amount < -1e-9;
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1526023Z  	
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1526079Z  	    IF negative_count > 0 THEN
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1526224Z  	        SELECT string_agg(format('(%s, %s, %s, %s)', id, product_id, stock_id, amount), ', ' ORDER BY id)
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1526282Z  	        INTO sample FROM (
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1526359Z  	            SELECT id, product_id, stock_id, amount
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1526427Z  	            FROM stock WHERE amount < -1e-9
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1526483Z  	            ORDER BY id LIMIT 10
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1526534Z  	        ) negative;
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1527002Z  	        RAISE EXCEPTION 'Migration refused: % stock rows hold a negative amount. Sample (stock id, product id, stock_id, amount): %. Choose an explicit repair and rerun migration. No stock has been deleted or changed beyond zeroing a residue within tolerance.', negative_count, sample
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1527191Z  	            USING HINT = 'List all rows: SELECT id, product_id, stock_id, amount FROM stock WHERE amount < -1e-9 ORDER BY id;';
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1527237Z  	    END IF;
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1527286Z  	END $$;
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1527333Z  	
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1527527Z  	ALTER TABLE stock ADD CONSTRAINT stock_amount_non_negative_check CHECK (amount >= 0);
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1527572Z  	
