2026-10-15T16:24:47.1537030Z  2026-10-15 16:19:06.475 UTC [4724] STATEMENT:  -- 2026-10-13 bug bash: chores.consume_product_on_execution is 0 or 1 (issue #923).
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1537078Z  	--
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1537132Z  	-- WHAT THIS CHANGES.
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1537282Z  	--   chores.consume_product_on_execution gets CHECK (consume_product_on_execution IN (0, 1)).
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1537432Z  	--   The column was SMALLINT NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 with no CHECK (migration 0084; upstream grocy has
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1537579Z  	--   none either), while its siblings (active, ...) are constrained, ChoresService tests the flag
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1537772Z  	--   with `== 1`, and the chore form writes 1 or 0. The generic POST/PUT /api/objects/chores
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1537911Z  	--   wrote any integer, so a 2 or a -1 meant "does not consume" without anyone having said so.
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1538007Z  	--   A write of any other value now fails with SQLSTATE 23514.
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1538054Z  	--
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1538202Z  	-- NULLABILITY. Unchanged, as the maintainer decided: the column is already NOT NULL and this
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1538347Z  	--   migration leaves that alone. The CHECK by itself would not reject NULL (NULL IN (0, 1) is
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1538455Z  	--   not false); the NOT NULL does, so there is no NULL case to preflight.
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1538502Z  	--
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1538640Z  	-- PREFLIGHT. The constraint is added only if no chore holds another value; otherwise the
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1538784Z  	--   migration is refused with a report and repairs nothing (ADR-0029). The constraint is added
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1538892Z  	--   validated, never NOT VALID, and no row is updated or deleted here.
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1538941Z  	--
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1539099Z  	-- PostgreSQL only, above DatabaseMigrationService::SQLITE_FROZEN_MIGRATION_ID, per ADR-0008's
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1539152Z  	-- retirement.
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1539199Z  	
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1539350Z  	-- ADR-0029: bounded blocking, validated atomically with the migration record. chores is small,
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1539505Z  	-- so the lock the ALTER needs anyway is taken up front instead of escalating to it after the check.
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1539564Z  	SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '5s';
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1539628Z  	SET LOCAL statement_timeout = '60s';
2026-10-15T16:24:47.1539697Z  	LOCK TABLE chores IN ACCESS EXCLUSIVE MODE;
